\begin{cases} b^2 - a^2 = 16 \\ a^2 + b^2 = 36 \end{cases}
\] Adding these two equations, we get \(2b^2 = 52\), so \(b^2 = 26\). Substituting \(b^2 = 26\) back into the first equation, we get \(26 - a^2 = 16\), so \(a^2 = 10\). Therefore, \(a = \sqrt{10}\) and \(b = \sqrt{26}\). The value of \(|ab|\) is \(\sqrt{10} \cdot \sqrt{26} = \sqrt{260} = 2\sqrt{65}\). </think> <answer> \(2\sqrt{65}\) </answer>

